# impeccable's design detector engine (specs/design-detector-in-bootstrap.md): one version of the
# npm platform package @impeccable/cli-linux-x64, placed by install/impeccable.sh (the bootstrap and
# CI's slow job run it) at ~/.impeccable/bin/<version>/impeccable, gstack's READY path.
# Format: <version> <sha256 of package/bin/impeccable, the binary itself>. The version is the npm
# package's, which gstack reads from the directory name and compares with the versions it has
# tested; the binary's own --version prints another number (impeccable's skills version, 4.0.0).
# The sha256 is the binary's, so it can be compared by eye with ENGINE_PINS['<version>']['linux-x64']
# in the pinned gstack's lib/design-detect-contract.ts (equal for 0.1.3, checked 2026-11-01).
# "gstack <commit>" names the gstack commit (install/gstack.pin) whose TESTED_ENGINE_VERSIONS and
# ENGINE_PINS this pin was checked against; tests/bootstrap.test.sh fails when the gstack pin moves
# without this line: re-check the engine against the new gstack, then update both.
